    <label>Example: Contact reporting line</label><protected>false</protected>
    <values><field>Record_Health_Check_Set__c</field><value
      xsi:type="xsd:string"
    >Example_Contact_Relationship_Readiness</value></values>
    <values><field>CheckTitle__c</field><value
      xsi:type="xsd:string"
    >Reporting Line Stays Within the Customer Account</value></values>
    <values><field>CheckDescription__c</field><value
      xsi:type="xsd:string"
    >When Reports To is used for an organizational chart, the manager should belong to the same Account as the Contact.</value></values>
    <values><field>EvaluationType__c</field><value
      xsi:type="xsd:string"
    >FORMULA</value></values>
    <values><field>PassConditionFormula__c</field><value
      xsi:type="xsd:string"
    >OR(ISBLANK(ReportsToId), ReportsTo.AccountId = AccountId)</value></values>
    <values><field>DisplayFoundFormula__c</field><value
      xsi:type="xsd:string"
    >IF(ISBLANK(ReportsToId), "No manager recorded", ReportsTo.Name)</value></values>
    <values><field>DisplayExpectedText__c</field><value
      xsi:type="xsd:string"
    >No manager, or a manager on the same Account</value></values>
    <values><field>FailureSeverity__c</field><value
      xsi:type="xsd:string"
    >INFO</value></values>
    <values><field>FailureMessage__c</field><value
      xsi:type="xsd:string"
    >{!record.Name fallback="This contact"} reports to a Contact on a different Account, which can distort the customer organization chart.</value></values>
    <values><field>FixMessage__c</field><value
      xsi:type="xsd:string"
    >Confirm the reporting relationship and Account assignments. Correct the inaccurate lookup or Account; do not remove a legitimate cross-company reporting relationship merely to pass the check.</value></values>
    <values><field>ActionLabel__c</field><value
      xsi:type="xsd:string"
    >Review reporting relationship</value></values>
